    "explanation": "Both parties: the 5.00 SGD no-show fee stands and is payable to the driver, so the ruling is DRIVER_COMPENSATION of 5.00 SGD (amount_sgd and driver_compensation_sgd both carry that one figure, POL-GEN-03), and the interim refund is reversed.\n\nDriver — your account is supported on the record. The trip was on-demand, so under POL-NS-21 the 300-second free wait ran from your arrival at 17:53:40 rather than from any scheduled time; it expired at 17:58:40, and you cancelled at 18:00:10 (390 s after arrival), so POL-NS-22's precondition is met. Your arrival is corroborated by the GPS trace (EV-GPS-05061): the vehicle is stationary at the Expo Hall 2 pickup from 17:53:30 through 18:00:00, the nearest fix is 26.2 m from the pickup point at 5 m reported accuracy, and 15 fixes fall inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE radius POL-NS-21 sets. You met POL-NS-23's contact obligation: two in-app messages (17:54:00 and 17:57:10, both delivered and read) and one in-app call (17:58:20, 35 s, unanswered), all before the 18:00:10 cancellation. The fare ledger (EV-FARE-05061) shows exactly 5.00 SGD, matching the POL-NS-22 schedule, so no fee-amount referral arises.\n\nRider — the points you raise do not defeat the charge. Your statement that the driver was not at the pickup point you set is contradicted by the GPS trace, which shows the vehicle dwelling at the venue pickup for the whole wait; the policy's own arrival test (trip record's arrival event corroborated by the trace within the LARGE_VENUE radius) is met, and reading the driver's messages does not establish that you were at the pickup and ready to board. Your statement that the driver 'never called' is contradicted by the platform's telemetry of an in-app call at 17:58:20 that rang 35 seconds unanswered, and POL-NS-23 makes the trip record the source of the contact facts. The absent traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-05061-01, status MISSING, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) carries no fact under POL-GEN-02(3), and no no-show rule needs traffic data, so it neither opens a POL-GEN-26 escalation nor helps either side. No repeat no-show referral arises: the rider snapshot does not carry no_show_cancellations_30d, so POL-NS-25 does not fire, and no goodwill credit is due because the driver did attempt contact (POL-NS-24).\n\nThe deciding facts — arrival, expiry of the free wait, and the contact obligation — are carried by EV-TRIP-05061, EV-GPS-05061, EV-CHAT-05061 and EV-FARE-05061, all COMPLETE at weight 1.0, so the confidence cap is 1.0; with a contested value of 5.00 SGD and no fraud flag, POL-GEN-22/POL-NS-26 require no minimum confidence and the AI ruling is final. Confidence is set at 0.90, not 1.0, to reflect the residual location-mismatch question that the venue-radius arrival test does not fully answer.",
